{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788373757239,"sessionID":"ses_f9c9e1f2effeUE9mG9h5hx4Ni7","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_01a06361ecc775c1a1b1dc17","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/TASK.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/TASK.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # REPAIR TASK\n2: \n3: A previous attempt at the task below is ALREADY in this directory but did NOT pass an independent evaluation. Read `FEEDBACK.md` for exactly what was wrong, then FIX the existing code so it builds, all tests run and pass, and every requirement is met. Do NOT start over.\n4: \n5: ---\n6: \n7: # Brazilian Soccer MCP Server - Specification\n8: \n9: ## Overview\n10: \n11: This document specifies the requirements for creating an MCP (Model Context Protocol) server that provides a knowledge graph interface for Brazilian soccer data. The server should enable natural language queries about players, teams, matches, and competitions using the provided datasets.\n12: \n13: ---\n14: \n15: ## Purpose\n16: \n17: - **Use Case**: Demo/Non-commercial use\n18: - **Goal**: Create an MCP server that can answer natural language questions about Brazilian soccer\n19: - **Integration**: MCP server connected to an LLM for query processing\n20: \n21: ---\n22: \n23: ## Provided Data\n24: \n25: The following datasets are included in `data/kaggle/` and must be used:\n26: \n27: ### Match Data\n28: \n29: #### 1. Brasileirão Serie A Matches\n30: **File**: `Brasileirao_Matches.csv` (4,180 matches)\n31: **Source**: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/ricardomattos05/jogos-do-campeonato-brasileiro\n32: **License**: CC BY 4.0\n33: \n34: | Column | Description |\n35: |--------|-------------|\n36: | datetime | Match date and time |\n37: | home_team | Home team name with state suffix (e.g., \"Palmeiras-SP\") |\n38: | home_team_state | State abbreviation |\n39: | away_team | Away team name with state suffix |\n40: | away_team_state | State abbreviation |\n41: | home_goal | Goals scored by home team |\n42: | away_goal | Goals scored by away team |\n43: | season | Year of the season |\n44: | round | Match round number |\n45: \n46: #### 2. Copa do Brasil Matches\n47: **File**: `Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv` (1,337 matches)\n48: **Source**: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/ricardomattos05/jogos-do-campeonato-brasileiro\n49: **License**: CC BY 4.0\n50: \n51: | Column | Description |\n52: |--------|-------------|\n53: | round | Cup round |\n54: | datetime | Match date and time |\n55: | home_team | Home team name |\n56: | away_team | Away team name |\n57: | home_goal | Home team goals |\n58: | away_goal | Away team goals |\n59: | season | Year |\n60: \n61: #### 3. Copa Libertadores Matches\n62: **File**: `Libertadores_Matches.csv` (1,255 matches)\n63: **Source**: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/ricardomattos05/jogos-do-campeonato-brasileiro\n64: **License**: CC BY 4.0\n65: \n66: | Column | Description |\n67: |--------|-------------|\n68: | datetime | Match date and time |\n69: | home_team | Home team name |\n70: | away_team | Away team name |\n71: | home_goal | Home team goals |\n72: | away_goal | Away team goals |\n73: | season | Year |\n74: | stage | Tournament stage (group stage, knockout, etc.) |\n75: \n76: #### 4. Extended Match Statistics\n77: **File**: `BR-Football-Dataset.csv` (10,296 matches)\n78: **Source**: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/cuecacuela/brazilian-football-matches\n79: **License**: CC0 Public Domain\n80: \n81: | Column | Description |\n82: |--------|-------------|\n83: | tournament | Competition name |\n84: | home | Home team |\n85: | away | Away team |\n86: | home_goal, away_goal | Final scores |\n87: | home_corner, away_corner | Corner kicks |\n88: | home_attack, away_attack | Attacks |\n89: | home_shots, away_shots | Shots |\n90: | time | Kick-off time |\n91: | date | Match date |\n92: | ht_result, at_result | Half-time results |\n93: | total_corners | Total corners in match |\n94: \n95: #### 5. Historical Brasileirão (2003-2019)\n96: **File**: `novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv` (6,886 matches)\n97: **Source**: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/macedojleo/campeonato-brasileiro-2003-a-2019\n98: **License**: CC BY 4.0\n99: \n100: | Column | Description |\n101: |--------|-------------|\n102: | ID | Unique match identifier |\n103: | Data | Match date (DD/MM/YYYY format) |\n104: | Ano | Year |\n105: | Rodada | Round number |\n106: | Equipe_mandante | Home team |\n107: | Equipe_visitante | Away team |\n108: | Gols_mandante | Home goals |\n109: | Gols_visitante | Away goals |\n110: | Mandante_UF, Visitante_UF | Team states |\n111: | Vencedor | Winner (Mandante/Visitante/Empate) |\n112: | Arena | Stadium name |\n113: \n114: ### Player Data\n115: \n116: #### 6. FIFA Player Database\n117: **File**: `fifa_data.csv` (18,207 players)\n118: **Source**: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/youssefelbadry10/fifa-players-data\n119: **License**: Apache 2.0\n120: \n121: Key columns include:\n122: | Column | Description |\n123: |--------|-------------|\n124: | ID | Unique player identifier |\n125: | Name | Player name |\n126: | Age | Player age |\n127: | Nationality | Country |\n128: | Overall | FIFA overall rating |\n129: | Potential | FIFA potential rating |\n130: | Club | Current club |\n131: | Position | Playing position |\n132: | Jersey Number | Shirt number |\n133: | Height, Weight | Physical attributes |\n134: | Various skill ratings | Crossing, Finishing, Dribbling, etc. |\n135: \n136: ---\n137: \n138: ## Additional Data Sources (Optional)\n139: \n140: These sources may be used to supplement the provided data:\n141: \n142: ### API-Football\n143: - **URL**: https://dashboard.api-football.com/\n144: - **Features**: Current season data, live scores\n145: - **Free tier**: Limited daily requests\n146: \n147: ### TheSportsDB\n148: - **URL**: https://www.thesportsdb.com/documentation\n149: - **Features**: Team logos, player photos, artwork\n150: - **Free tier**: Test key \"123\", 2 requests/minute limit\n151: \n152: ### Wikipedia/DBpedia\n153: - Historical context and notable player/team information\n154: \n155: ---\n156: \n157: ## Required Capabilities\n158: \n159: The MCP server must support queries in these categories:\n160: \n161: ### 1. Match Queries\n162: \n163: **Find matches by criteria:**\n164: - By team (home, away, or either)\n165: - By date range\n166: - By competition (Brasileirão, Copa do Brasil, Libertadores)\n167: - By season\n168: \n169: **Example questions:**\n170: - \"Show me all Flamengo vs Fluminense matches\"\n171: - \"What matches did Palmeiras play in 2023?\"\n172: - \"Find all Copa do Brasil finals\"\n173: \n174: **Example answer format:**\n175: ```\n176: Flamengo vs Fluminense (Fla-Flu derby):\n177: - 2023-09-03: Flamengo 2-1 Fluminense (Brasileirão Round 22)\n178: - 2023-05-28: Fluminense 1-0 Flamengo (Brasileirão Round 8)\n179: - ... (15 more matches in dataset)\n180: \n181: Head-to-head in dataset: Flamengo 12 wins, Fluminense 8 wins, 7 draws\n182: ```\n183: \n184: ### 2. Team Queries\n185: \n186: **Find team information:**\n187: - Match history and statistics\n188: - Win/loss/draw records\n189: - Goals scored/conceded\n190: - Performance by competition\n191: \n192: **Example questions:**\n193: - \"What is Corinthians' home record in 2022?\"\n194: - \"Which team scored the most goals in Serie A 2023?\"\n195: - \"Compare Palmeiras and Santos head-to-head\"\n196: \n197: **Example answer format:**\n198: ```\n199: Corinthians home record (2022 Brasileirão):\n200: - Matches: 19\n201: - Wins: 11, Draws: 5, Losses: 3\n202: - Goals For: 28, Goals Against: 15\n203: - Win rate: 57.9%\n204: ```\n205: \n206: ### 3. Player Queries\n207: \n208: **Find player information:**\n209: - Search by name\n210: - Filter by nationality (especially Brazilian players)\n211: - Filter by club (especially Brazilian clubs)\n212: - Player ratings and attributes\n213: \n214: **Example questions:**\n215: - \"Find all Brazilian players in the dataset\"\n216: - \"Who are the highest-rated players at Flamengo?\"\n217: - \"Show me all forwards from São Paulo FC\"\n218: \n219: **Example answer format:**\n220: ```\n221: Top-rated Brazilian players in dataset:\n222: 1. Neymar Jr - Overall: 92, Position: LW, Club: Paris Saint-Germain\n223: 2. Alisson - Overall: 89, Position: GK, Club: Liverpool\n224: 3. Casemiro - Overall: 89, Position: CDM, Club: Real Madrid\n225: ...\n226: \n227: Brazilian players at Brazilian clubs:\n228: - Flamengo: 8 players (avg rating: 74)\n229: - Palmeiras: 7 players (avg rating: 72)\n230: ...\n231: ```\n232: \n233: ### 4. Competition Queries\n234: \n235: **Find competition information:**\n236: - Standings by season (calculated from match results)\n237: - Top scorers (if inferable from data)\n238: - Match schedules and results\n239: \n240: **Example questions:**\n241: - \"Who won the 2019 Brasileirão?\"\n242: - \"Show the 2018 Copa Libertadores bracket\"\n243: - \"Which teams were relegated in 2020?\"\n244: \n245: **Example answer format:**\n246: ```\n247: 2019 Brasileirão Final Standings (calculated from matches):\n248: 1. Flamengo - 90 pts (28W, 6D, 4L) - Champion\n249: 2. Santos - 74 pts (22W, 8D, 8L)\n250: 3. Palmeiras - 74 pts (21W, 11D, 6L)\n251: ...\n252: ```\n253: \n254: ### 5. Statistical Analysis\n255: \n256: **Calculate aggregated statistics:**\n257: - Goals per match averages\n258: - Team performance trends\n259: - Head-to-head records\n260: - Home vs away performance\n261: \n262: **Example questions:**\n263: - \"What's the average goals per match in the Brasileirão?\"\n264: - \"Which team has the best away record?\"\n265: - \"Show me the biggest wins in the dataset\"\n266: \n267: **Example answer format:**\n268: ```\n269: Biggest victories in Brasileirão (provided data):\n270: 1. 2012-05-27: Santos 8-0 Bolivar (Libertadores)\n271: 2. 2015-09-13: Palmeiras 6-0 São Paulo\n272: 3. 2019-10-27: Flamengo 5-0 Grêmio\n273: ...\n274: \n275: Average goals per match: 2.47\n276: Home win rate: 47.3%\n277: ```\n278: \n279: ---\n280: \n281: ## Sample Questions and Expected Behaviors\n282: \n283: ### Simple Lookups\n284: | Question | Expected Behavior |\n285: |----------|-------------------|\n286: | \"When did Flamengo last play Corinthians?\" | Search match data for most recent match between these teams |\n287: | \"What was the score?\" | Return home_goal and away_goal |\n288: | \"Who is Gabriel Barbosa?\" | Search FIFA player data by name |\n289: \n290: ### Relationship Queries\n291: | Question | Expected Behavior |\n292: |----------|-------------------|\n293: | \"Which players play for Flamengo?\" | Filter FIFA data by Club containing \"Flamengo\" |\n294: | \"Show me all derbies in 2023\" | Find matches where teams are traditional rivals |\n295: | \"What competitions has Palmeiras played in?\" | Search all match files for Palmeiras matches |\n296: \n297: ### Analytical Queries\n298: | Question | Expected Behavior |\n299: |----------|-------------------|\n300: | \"Which team has the best home record?\" | Calculate win rates from match data |\n301: | \"Who are the top Brazilian players?\" | Filter and sort FIFA data |\n302: | \"Compare the 2018 and 2019 seasons\" | Aggregate statistics across seasons |\n303: \n304: ---\n305: \n306: ## Data Quality Notes\n307: \n308: ### Team Name Variations\n309: The datasets use different naming conventions:\n310: - With state suffix: \"Palmeiras-SP\", \"Flamengo-RJ\"\n311: - Without suffix: \"Palmeiras\", \"Flamengo\"\n312: - Full names: \"Sport Club Corinthians Paulista\"\n313: \n314: **Implementation should normalize team names for consistent matching.**\n315: \n316: ### Date Formats\n317: - ISO format: \"2023-09-24\"\n318: - Brazilian format: \"29/03/2003\"\n319: - With time: \"2012-05-19 18:30:00\"\n320: \n321: **Implementation should handle multiple date formats.**\n322: \n323: ### Character Encoding\n324: Brazilian Portuguese text includes special characters:\n325: - Accents: São Paulo, Grêmio, Avaí\n326: - Cedilla: Fortaleza Esporte Clube\n327: \n328: **Implementation should handle UTF-8 encoding.**\n329: \n330: ---\n331: \n332: ## Success Criteria\n333: \n334: ### Functional Requirements\n335: - [ ] Can search and return match data from all provided CSV files\n336: - [ ] Can search and return player data\n337: - [ ] Can calculate basic statistics (wins, losses, goals)\n338: - [ ] Can compare teams head-to-head\n339: - [ ] Handles team name variations correctly\n340: - [ ] Returns properly formatted responses\n341: \n342: ### Query Performance\n343: - [ ] Simple lookups respond in < 2 seconds\n344: - [ ] Aggregate queries respond in < 5 seconds\n345: - [ ] No timeout errors\n346: \n347: ### Data Coverage\n348: - [ ] All 6 CSV files are loadable and queryable\n349: - [ ] At least 20 sample questions can be answered\n350: - [ ] Cross-file queries work (e.g., player + match data)\n351: \n352: ---\n353: \n354: ## Testing Approach\n355: \n356: Use BDD (Behavior-Driven Development) test scenarios:\n357: \n358: ```gherkin\n359: Feature: Match Queries\n360: \n361: Scenario: Find matches between two teams\n362:   Given the match data is loaded\n363:   When I search for matches between \"Flamengo\" and \"Fluminense\"\n364:   Then I should receive a list of matches\n365:   And each match should have date, scores, and competition\n366: \n367: Scenario: Get team statistics\n368:   Given the match data is loaded\n369:   When I request statistics for \"Palmeiras\" in season \"2023\"\n370:   Then I should receive wins, losses, draws, and goals\n371: ```\n372: \n373: ---\n374: \n375: ## Document Information\n376: - **Version**: 2.0\n377: - **Purpose**: Specification for Brazilian Soccer MCP Server benchmark\n378: - **Data**: Pre-downloaded Kaggle datasets included in repository\n379: - **Status**: Ready for implementation\n380: \n381: ---\n382: \n383: ## References\n384: \n385: ### MCP Protocol\n386: - Documentation: https://modelcontextprotocol.io\n387: \n388: ### Data Sources\n389: - Kaggle Brazilian Soccer: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/ricardomattos05/jogos-do-campeonato-brasileiro\n390: - Brazilian Football Matches: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/cuecacuela/brazilian-football-matches\n391: - Campeonato Brasileiro 2003-2019: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/macedojleo/campeonato-brasileiro-2003-a-2019\n392: - FIFA Players: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/youssefelbadry10/fifa-players-data\n393: \n394: ### Optional APIs\n395: - API-Football: https://dashboard.api-football.com/\n396: - TheSportsDB: https://www.thesportsdb.com/documentation\n\n(End of file - total 396 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# REPAIR TASK\n\nA previous attempt at the task below is ALREADY in this directory but did NOT pass an independent evaluation. Read `FEEDBACK.md` for exactly what was wrong, then FIX the existing code so it builds, all tests run and pass, and every requirement is met. Do NOT start over.\n\n---\n\n# Brazilian Soccer MCP Server - Specification\n\n## Overview\n\nThis document specifies the requirements for creating an MCP (Model Context Protocol) server that provides a knowledge graph interface for Brazilian soccer data. The server should enable natural language queries about players, teams, matches, and competitions using the provided datasets.\n\n---\n\n## Purpose\n\n- **Use Case**: Demo/Non-commercial use\n- **Goal**: Create an MCP server that can answer natural language questions about Brazilian soccer\n- **Integration**: MCP server connected to an LLM for query processing\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/TASK.md","text":"# REPAIR TASK\n\nA previous attempt at the task below is ALREADY in this directory but did NOT pass an independent evaluation. Read `FEEDBACK.md` for exactly what was wrong, then FIX the existing code so it builds, all tests run and pass, and every requirement is met. Do NOT start over.\n\n---\n\n# Brazilian Soccer MCP Server - Specification\n\n## Overview\n\nThis document specifies the requirements for creating an MCP (Model Context Protocol) server that provides a knowledge graph interface for Brazilian soccer data. The server should enable natural language queries about players, teams, matches, and competitions using the provided datasets.\n\n---\n\n## Purpose\n\n- **Use Case**: Demo/Non-commercial use\n- **Goal**: Create an MCP server that can answer natural language questions about Brazilian soccer\n- **Integration**: MCP server connected to an LLM for query processing\n\n---\n\n## Provided Data\n\nThe following datasets are included in `data/kaggle/` and must be used:\n\n### Match Data\n\n#### 1. Brasileirão Serie A Matches\n**File**: `Brasileirao_Matches.csv` (4,180 matches)\n**Source**: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/ricardomattos05/jogos-do-campeonato-brasileiro\n**License**: CC BY 4.0\n\n| Column | Description |\n|--------|-------------|\n| datetime | Match date and time |\n| home_team | Home team name with state suffix (e.g., \"Palmeiras-SP\") |\n| home_team_state | State abbreviation |\n| away_team | Away team name with state suffix |\n| away_team_state | State abbreviation |\n| home_goal | Goals scored by home team |\n| away_goal | Goals scored by away team |\n| season | Year of the season |\n| round | Match round number |\n\n#### 2. Copa do Brasil Matches\n**File**: `Brazilian_Cup_Matches.csv` (1,337 matches)\n**Source**: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/ricardomattos05/jogos-do-campeonato-brasileiro\n**License**: CC BY 4.0\n\n| Column | Description |\n|--------|-------------|\n| round | Cup round |\n| datetime | Match date and time |\n| home_team | Home team name |\n| away_team | Away team name |\n| home_goal | Home team goals |\n| away_goal | Away team goals |\n| season | Year |\n\n#### 3. Copa Libertadores Matches\n**File**: `Libertadores_Matches.csv` (1,255 matches)\n**Source**: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/ricardomattos05/jogos-do-campeonato-brasileiro\n**License**: CC BY 4.0\n\n| Column | Description |\n|--------|-------------|\n| datetime | Match date and time |\n| home_team | Home team name |\n| away_team | Away team name |\n| home_goal | Home team goals |\n| away_goal | Away team goals |\n| season | Year |\n| stage | Tournament stage (group stage, knockout, etc.) |\n\n#### 4. Extended Match Statistics\n**File**: `BR-Football-Dataset.csv` (10,296 matches)\n**Source**: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/cuecacuela/brazilian-football-matches\n**License**: CC0 Public Domain\n\n| Column | Description |\n|--------|-------------|\n| tournament | Competition name |\n| home | Home team |\n| away | Away team |\n| home_goal, away_goal | Final scores |\n| home_corner, away_corner | Corner kicks |\n| home_attack, away_attack | Attacks |\n| home_shots, away_shots | Shots |\n| time | Kick-off time |\n| date | Match date |\n| ht_result, at_result | Half-time results |\n| total_corners | Total corners in match |\n\n#### 5. Historical Brasileirão (2003-2019)\n**File**: `novo_campeonato_brasileiro.csv` (6,886 matches)\n**Source**: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/macedojleo/campeonato-brasileiro-2003-a-2019\n**License**: CC BY 4.0\n\n| Column | Description |\n|--------|-------------|\n| ID | Unique match identifier |\n| Data | Match date (DD/MM/YYYY format) |\n| Ano | Year |\n| Rodada | Round number |\n| Equipe_mandante | Home team |\n| Equipe_visitante | Away team |\n| Gols_mandante | Home goals |\n| Gols_visitante | Away goals |\n| Mandante_UF, Visitante_UF | Team states |\n| Vencedor | Winner (Mandante/Visitante/Empate) |\n| Arena | Stadium name |\n\n### Player Data\n\n#### 6. FIFA Player Database\n**File**: `fifa_data.csv` (18,207 players)\n**Source**: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/youssefelbadry10/fifa-players-data\n**License**: Apache 2.0\n\nKey columns include:\n| Column | Description |\n|--------|-------------|\n| ID | Unique player identifier |\n| Name | Player name |\n| Age | Player age |\n| Nationality | Country |\n| Overall | FIFA overall rating |\n| Potential | FIFA potential rating |\n| Club | Current club |\n| Position | Playing position |\n| Jersey Number | Shirt number |\n| Height, Weight | Physical attributes |\n| Various skill ratings | Crossing, Finishing, Dribbling, etc. |\n\n---\n\n## Additional Data Sources (Optional)\n\nThese sources may be used to supplement the provided data:\n\n### API-Football\n- **URL**: https://dashboard.api-football.com/\n- **Features**: Current season data, live scores\n- **Free tier**: Limited daily requests\n\n### TheSportsDB\n- **URL**: https://www.thesportsdb.com/documentation\n- **Features**: Team logos, player photos, artwork\n- **Free tier**: Test key \"123\", 2 requests/minute limit\n\n### Wikipedia/DBpedia\n- Historical context and notable player/team information\n\n---\n\n## Required Capabilities\n\nThe MCP server must support queries in these categories:\n\n### 1. Match Queries\n\n**Find matches by criteria:**\n- By team (home, away, or either)\n- By date range\n- By competition (Brasileirão, Copa do Brasil, Libertadores)\n- By season\n\n**Example questions:**\n- \"Show me all Flamengo vs Fluminense matches\"\n- \"What matches did Palmeiras play in 2023?\"\n- \"Find all Copa do Brasil finals\"\n\n**Example answer format:**\n```\nFlamengo vs Fluminense (Fla-Flu derby):\n- 2023-09-03: Flamengo 2-1 Fluminense (Brasileirão Round 22)\n- 2023-05-28: Fluminense 1-0 Flamengo (Brasileirão Round 8)\n- ... (15 more matches in dataset)\n\nHead-to-head in dataset: Flamengo 12 wins, Fluminense 8 wins, 7 draws\n```\n\n### 2. Team Queries\n\n**Find team information:**\n- Match history and statistics\n- Win/loss/draw records\n- Goals scored/conceded\n- Performance by competition\n\n**Example questions:**\n- \"What is Corinthians' home record in 2022?\"\n- \"Which team scored the most goals in Serie A 2023?\"\n- \"Compare Palmeiras and Santos head-to-head\"\n\n**Example answer format:**\n```\nCorinthians home record (2022 Brasileirão):\n- Matches: 19\n- Wins: 11, Draws: 5, Losses: 3\n- Goals For: 28, Goals Against: 15\n- Win rate: 57.9%\n```\n\n### 3. Player Queries\n\n**Find player information:**\n- Search by name\n- Filter by nationality (especially Brazilian players)\n- Filter by club (especially Brazilian clubs)\n- Player ratings and attributes\n\n**Example questions:**\n- \"Find all Brazilian players in the dataset\"\n- \"Who are the highest-rated players at Flamengo?\"\n- \"Show me all forwards from São Paulo FC\"\n\n**Example answer format:**\n```\nTop-rated Brazilian players in dataset:\n1. Neymar Jr - Overall: 92, Position: LW, Club: Paris Saint-Germain\n2. Alisson - Overall: 89, Position: GK, Club: Liverpool\n3. Casemiro - Overall: 89, Position: CDM, Club: Real Madrid\n...\n\nBrazilian players at Brazilian clubs:\n- Flamengo: 8 players (avg rating: 74)\n- Palmeiras: 7 players (avg rating: 72)\n...\n```\n\n### 4. Competition Queries\n\n**Find competition information:**\n- Standings by season (calculated from match results)\n- Top scorers (if inferable from data)\n- Match schedules and results\n\n**Example questions:**\n- \"Who won the 2019 Brasileirão?\"\n- \"Show the 2018 Copa Libertadores bracket\"\n- \"Which teams were relegated in 2020?\"\n\n**Example answer format:**\n```\n2019 Brasileirão Final Standings (calculated from matches):\n1. Flamengo - 90 pts (28W, 6D, 4L) - Champion\n2. Santos - 74 pts (22W, 8D, 8L)\n3. Palmeiras - 74 pts (21W, 11D, 6L)\n...\n```\n\n### 5. Statistical Analysis\n\n**Calculate aggregated statistics:**\n- Goals per match averages\n- Team performance trends\n- Head-to-head records\n- Home vs away performance\n\n**Example questions:**\n- \"What's the average goals per match in the Brasileirão?\"\n- \"Which team has the best away record?\"\n- \"Show me the biggest wins in the dataset\"\n\n**Example answer format:**\n```\nBiggest victories in Brasileirão (provided data):\n1. 2012-05-27: Santos 8-0 Bolivar (Libertadores)\n2. 2015-09-13: Palmeiras 6-0 São Paulo\n3. 2019-10-27: Flamengo 5-0 Grêmio\n...\n\nAverage goals per match: 2.47\nHome win rate: 47.3%\n```\n\n---\n\n## Sample Questions and Expected Behaviors\n\n### Simple Lookups\n| Question | Expected Behavior |\n|----------|-------------------|\n| \"When did Flamengo last play Corinthians?\" | Search match data for most recent match between these teams |\n| \"What was the score?\" | Return home_goal and away_goal |\n| \"Who is Gabriel Barbosa?\" | Search FIFA player data by name |\n\n### Relationship Queries\n| Question | Expected Behavior |\n|----------|-------------------|\n| \"Which players play for Flamengo?\" | Filter FIFA data by Club containing \"Flamengo\" |\n| \"Show me all derbies in 2023\" | Find matches where teams are traditional rivals |\n| \"What competitions has Palmeiras played in?\" | Search all match files for Palmeiras matches |\n\n### Analytical Queries\n| Question | Expected Behavior |\n|----------|-------------------|\n| \"Which team has the best home record?\" | Calculate win rates from match data |\n| \"Who are the top Brazilian players?\" | Filter and sort FIFA data |\n| \"Compare the 2018 and 2019 seasons\" | Aggregate statistics across seasons |\n\n---\n\n## Data Quality Notes\n\n### Team Name Variations\nThe datasets use different naming conventions:\n- With state suffix: \"Palmeiras-SP\", \"Flamengo-RJ\"\n- Without suffix: \"Palmeiras\", \"Flamengo\"\n- Full names: \"Sport Club Corinthians Paulista\"\n\n**Implementation should normalize team names for consistent matching.**\n\n### Date Formats\n- ISO format: \"2023-09-24\"\n- Brazilian format: \"29/03/2003\"\n- With time: \"2012-05-19 18:30:00\"\n\n**Implementation should handle multiple date formats.**\n\n### Character Encoding\nBrazilian Portuguese text includes special characters:\n- Accents: São Paulo, Grêmio, Avaí\n- Cedilla: Fortaleza Esporte Clube\n\n**Implementation should handle UTF-8 encoding.**\n\n---\n\n## Success Criteria\n\n### Functional Requirements\n- [ ] Can search and return match data from all provided CSV files\n- [ ] Can search and return player data\n- [ ] Can calculate basic statistics (wins, losses, goals)\n- [ ] Can compare teams head-to-head\n- [ ] Handles team name variations correctly\n- [ ] Returns properly formatted responses\n\n### Query Performance\n- [ ] Simple lookups respond in < 2 seconds\n- [ ] Aggregate queries respond in < 5 seconds\n- [ ] No timeout errors\n\n### Data Coverage\n- [ ] All 6 CSV files are loadable and queryable\n- [ ] At least 20 sample questions can be answered\n- [ ] Cross-file queries work (e.g., player + match data)\n\n---\n\n## Testing Approach\n\nUse BDD (Behavior-Driven Development) test scenarios:\n\n```gherkin\nFeature: Match Queries\n\nScenario: Find matches between two teams\n  Given the match data is loaded\n  When I search for matches between \"Flamengo\" and \"Fluminense\"\n  Then I should receive a list of matches\n  And each match should have date, scores, and competition\n\nScenario: Get team statistics\n  Given the match data is loaded\n  When I request statistics for \"Palmeiras\" in season \"2023\"\n  Then I should receive wins, losses, draws, and goals\n```\n\n---\n\n## Document Information\n- **Version**: 2.0\n- **Purpose**: Specification for Brazilian Soccer MCP Server benchmark\n- **Data**: Pre-downloaded Kaggle datasets included in repository\n- **Status**: Ready for implementation\n\n---\n\n## References\n\n### MCP Protocol\n- Documentation: https://modelcontextprotocol.io\n\n### Data Sources\n- Kaggle Brazilian Soccer: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/ricardomattos05/jogos-do-campeonato-brasileiro\n- Brazilian Football Matches: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/cuecacuela/brazilian-football-matches\n- Campeonato Brasileiro 2003-2019: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/macedojleo/campeonato-brasileiro-2003-a-2019\n- FIFA Players: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/youssefelbadry10/fifa-players-data\n\n### Optional APIs\n- API-Football: https://dashboard.api-football.com/\n- TheSportsDB: https://www.thesportsdb.com/documentation","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":396,"totalLines":396,"truncated":false}},"title":"TASK.md","time":{"start":1788373757177,"end":1788373757229}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Let me start by reading the TASK.md file.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_06361ecda001KeQiXip5YMRvqn","sessionID":"ses_f9c9e1f2effeUE9mG9h5hx4Ni7","messageID":"msg_06361e57b001dtmtamyxTvp404"}}
